  "details": "My Avatar Pedestals were not working and it was missing items under \"Interaction\" field. Upon checking SDK's InteractToggle.cs and the Udon assembly, i realized the \"Interact\" in the script getting changed into lowercase \"ınteract\" in assembly, resulting with a non English character \"ı\", and thus not working as intended.\n\nThis issue affects every script that uses capital i (I) character as a modifier when operating system is set to Turkish.\n\nI hope VRC team can make changes on how Udon creates assembly, so it can copy the names of modifiers without changing formatting and use 1 to 1 from C# scripts.",
